| `http_client` speaks first: a request that never got a response also pushes an
| `Exception` particle into the program, dispatched to the program's own
| handler between top-level statements.
|
| The `ok: false` value is unchanged and still complete on its own — the
| push is additional, never instead of it. A program that ignores
| diagnostics loses nothing, which net_unreachable.code proves by defining
| no handler at all and passing anyway.
|
| Port 1 is privileged and never bound, so the refusal is immediate and
| this fixture needs no network.
link "native_modules/http_client.so" as http

let reported = ""

Exception { source, message } => {
    reported = source
}

emit Get { url = "http://127.0.0.1:1/" } to http get r
assert not r.ok
assert r.status = 0

| Draining happens between top-level statements, so the handler has already
| run by the time this line does.
assert reported = "http_client"
